Dear Bo Alstrup,

My name is Theo van der Greft and I work as an IT specialist at Connect2Mus=
ic.
Connect2music aims to stimulate people with a visual disability, to practic=
e music or singing. For example, we organize workshops and provide professi=
onals in education about aids for the practice of music by people with a vi=
sual impairment.
Another spearhead is to make it possible to convert sheet music to enlargem=
ent or Braille.
On the website of IBOS we found information about the MusicXMLReader. We ha=
ve made a link to this on our website (https://www.connect2music.nl/index.p=
hp/bladmuziek)
We have received a response from a number of users that unfortunately they =
cannot use this program because their PC is running on Linux or MAC OS.
I see on your website that one of the future developments is making the sof=
tware available on other platforms, like Android, iOS, and MAC OS. 

My question is whether it is possible in the future to develop a web applic=
ation, so that it can be used from any platform. If that is technically pos=
sible, we are willing to find out in which way we can help you to realize t=
his.

 

Greetings,

Theo van der Greft


